# Streaming follow-ups

- `completion_coordinator.py` and `descendant_evidence.py`: characterize the
  race between a final descendant refresh and terminal publication before
  deciding whether spawn admission needs a stronger closing protocol.
- `pi_drain.py` and `pi_quiescence.py`: establish a paired native lifecycle
  signal before supporting arbitrary branch-summary work; queue updates and
  retry telemetry cannot establish busy or idle on their own.
- `resident_drain.py`: on a hold with no native task source, if exhausted rearm
  budgets occur in practice, recapture the report after the child's next successful
  turn; its later text cannot replace the retained candidate without a rearm.
